assess_fluid_balance, assess_infusions, assess_medications, assess_pathology,
assess_mobility, assess_skin_integrity,
rec_discharge_plan, rec_actions, rec_plan, rec_patient_goals

WORKFLOW (use this every time)
1) Read the whole transcript once.
2) Do a second pass and extract explicit statements into buckets: Situation / Background / Assessment / Recommendations.
3) For each category key, ask: “Is there a direct statement that satisfies the definition below?”
4) Add label ONLY if yes; otherwise omit.
5) Return JSON only.

CATEGORY DEFINITIONS & BOUNDARIES (domain-specific; be strict)

INTRO/INVITE/ID
- introduction_patients:
  - Clinician introduces self to patient (“Hi Bill, I’m Sam…”) OR introduces the patient in bedside context (“This is Bill…”).
  - Note: “This is Sam, taking over” said in front of patient counts as introduction_patients (it introduces the incoming nurse to the patient).
- introduction_clinicians:
  - Clinicians explicitly introduce/identify each other as part of handover (“This is Sam taking over from me”, “I’m handing over to Evie”).
  - A nurse stating only their own name to the patient is NOT introduction_clinicians.
- invitation:
  - Explicit permission/invitation for bedside handover and/or patient participation (“Is it okay if we do bedside handover?”, “Please jump in…”).
- id_check (VERY STRICT):
  - Label ONLY if ALL THREE are checked in the transcript: (1) name AND (2) date of birth AND (3) an ID number/URN/MRN.
  - Name only or name+DOB is NOT enough. “ID band matches” without a number is NOT enough.

SITUATION
- sit_diagnosis:
  - Explicit reason for admission/primary problem/procedure context (e.g., “severe tonsillitis”, “post–brain surgery”, “known cancer and recent brain injury”).
- sit_events:
  - Explicit significant events/complications that occurred (e.g., desaturation episode, fall, pneumothorax, bleeding episode). Tests ordered alone are not events.
- sit_status:
  - Explicit current state/stage or what they are awaiting/what is happening now (e.g., “heading to theatre later this morning”, “day 2 post‑op”, “awaiting surgical team review”, “less drowsy than earlier”, “stable overnight”).

BACKGROUND
- bg_history:
  - Explicit comorbidities or relevant past history stated as background (e.g., “known cancer”, CKD, bradycardia).
- bg_allergies:
  - Explicit allergies OR explicitly “no known allergies/NKDA”.
- bg_fall_risk / bg_pi_risk:
  - Only if risk is explicitly mentioned (falls/pressure injury risk tools or statements).
- bg_acp:
  - Only if advance care planning / goals-of-care / resus status explicitly mentioned.

ASSESSMENT (what is/was assessed; do not confuse with plans)
- assess_obs:
  - Actual vitals/observations listed OR explicit statement “obs/vitals stable”.
- assess_monitoring (DO NOT over-label):
  - Only if special monitoring beyond routine observations is explicitly mentioned (telemetry, neuro checks, alarms, strict frequency like hourly neuro obs as an active monitoring order).
  - Routine “continue obs”, “check obs”, or “obs stable” => assess_obs only.
- assess_pain:
  - Pain discussed/asked/scored OR pain control described (“significant throat pain”, “pain well controlled”, “due for analgesia”).
- assess_devices:
  - Explicit devices/lines/tubes/drains (PIVC/cannula with gauge/site, IDC/catheter, drain, chest tube, CVC, etc.).
  - Note: “IV fluids running” alone is NOT a device; that is an infusion.
- assess_infusions (commonly missed; be proactive):
  - Explicit infusion running and/or rate/continuous IV therapy (“IV fluids running”, “ongoing IV fluids at 125 mL/hr”, “NS at 75 mL/hr”).
  - Does NOT require a cannula mention.
- assess_medications (be precise):
  - Only if specific meds/therapy types are explicitly mentioned (e.g., antibiotics, analgesia, PCA, named drugs, PRNs charted).
  - “Medication review” without naming meds => DO NOT label.
  - If antibiotics/analgesia are mentioned generally, that still counts as medications (e.g., “antibiotics”, “analgesia now”).
- assess_nutrition (commonly missed):
  - Diet status/intake permissions or restrictions (NBM, allowed to eat/drink, general diet, tolerating sips).
- assess_fluid_balance:
  - I/O balance, urine output, daily weights, fluid restriction (NOT just “IV fluids running”).
- assess_pathology:
  - Labs/imaging/cultures: results OR pending/ordered tests explicitly stated.
- assess_mobility:
  - Mobility/assistance/ambulation/physio details explicitly stated.
- assess_skin_integrity (commonly missed):
  - Wounds/dressings/pressure areas/skin condition explicitly stated (e.g., “dressing clean/dry/intact”, “bone flap dressing left intact”).

RECOMMENDATIONS / PLAN
- rec_plan:
  - General plan/follow-ups for the shift/day (continue obs schedule, maintain IV fluids, give antibiotics after lunch, keep dressing intact until review, “keep an eye on…”).
  - Plans can be stated by either nurse; if it’s a clear intended action/continuation, label it.
- rec_actions (DO NOT over-label):
  - Only if explicitly urgent/time-critical escalation (e.g., “call team immediately if…”, “stat”, “must do now”, “urgent escalation”).
  - Routine “give next dose later”, “continue”, “monitor” => rec_plan (NOT rec_actions).
- rec_discharge_plan:
  - Explicit discharge/transfer/placement planning.
- rec_patient_goals (commonly missed):
  - Explicit elicitation of patient needs/preferences or immediate goals (“Anything you need right now?”, “Are you comfortable?”, “Are you feeling up to lunch?”, “Buzz if you need anything” when it clearly invites needs/requests).

COMMON ERROR TRAPS (avoid these)
- Do NOT label id_check unless name + DOB + MRN/URN/ID number are all verified.
- Do NOT label assess_monitoring for “obs stable” or “continue obs” alone.
- Do NOT label rec_actions for routine tasks; urgency must be explicit.
- Do NOT miss:
  - assess_infusions when any IV fluids/rate are mentioned,
  - assess_nutrition when NBM/allowed to eat & drink is mentioned,
  - bg_allergies when NKDA/allergies are stated,
  - assess_skin_integrity when dressings/wounds are described,
  - introduction_patients when the nurse introduces themselves to the patient,
  - rec_patient_goals when patient comfort/needs/preferences are explicitly asked.

Return JSON only: {"labels":[...]} with zero extra text.
