2026/02/21 08:54:14 INFO dspy.teleprompt.gepa.gepa: Iteration 17: Proposed new text for self: text
You are given a transcript of a clinical bedside handover (outgoing→incoming nurse; may include patient/carer). Your task is to output which handover categories are EXPLICITLY addressed in the transcript.

CORE PRINCIPLE (STRICT)
- Label ONLY if the transcript contains a clear, direct statement that matches the category definition.
- Do NOT infer, assume, or “read between the lines”.
- When unsure, do not label (prefer under-labeling).

MANDATORY OUTPUT FORMAT
- Return ONLY a JSON object exactly like: {"labels":[...]}
- "labels" must be a JSON array of strings.
- Each string MUST be EXACTLY one of the category keys listed below.
- No extra keys, no explanations, no markdown, no commentary.

CATEGORY KEYS (only these)
introduction_clinicians, introduction_patients, invitation, id_check,
sit_diagnosis, sit_events, sit_status,
bg_history, bg_fall_risk, bg_pi_risk, bg_allergies, bg_acp,
assess_obs, assess_pain, assess_devices, assess_monitoring, assess_nutrition,
assess_fluid_balance, assess_infusions, assess_medications, assess_pathology,
assess_mobility, assess_skin_integrity,
rec_discharge_plan, rec_actions, rec_plan, rec_patient_goals

WORKFLOW (do this systematically)
1) Read the whole transcript once.
2) Second pass: for each category, ask “Is there an explicit statement that matches this category?”
3) Add label only if YES.
4) Output JSON only.

CATEGORY DECISION RULES (high-importance, error-prone)

A) Situation (SIT)
- sit_diagnosis: explicit reason for admission/primary problem/procedure context (e.g., “admitted with gastroenteritis”, “CCF exacerbation”, “for pericardiocentesis”).
- sit_events: explicit adverse/significant events that occurred (e.g., fall, desaturation episode, complication). Tests being ordered or “bloods taken” alone is NOT an event.
- sit_status: only if current phase/state is explicitly stated (e.g., “day 2 post-op”, “awaiting procedure this afternoon”, “reviewed this morning”, “stable overnight”). Do not label just because a plan exists.

B) Background (BG)
- bg_history: explicit comorbidities or relevant past history stated as history/background (e.g., CKD, diabetes, EF 30%, “no known medical history” counts as explicit background).
- bg_allergies: label if allergies are explicitly stated, including “NKDA / no known allergies”.
- bg_fall_risk, bg_pi_risk, bg_acp: label only if explicitly mentioned.

C) Assessment (ASSESS) — strict boundaries
- assess_obs: any vitals/observations OR explicit statement like “obs/vitals stable”. Includes O2 requirement/sats when stated.
- assess_monitoring: ONLY special monitoring beyond routine obs (telemetry, neuro checks, alarms, hourly neuro obs). “Continue obs”, “monitor” or “obs stable” is NOT assess_monitoring.
- assess_devices: explicit device/line/drain mention (e.g., cannula/PIVC with gauge/location, CVC, IDC/catheter, drain, chest tube).
- assess_infusions: explicit infusion running and/or rate/continuous IV therapy (e.g., “IV fluids running”, “NS at 75 mL/hr”, “maintenance IV fluids”). Do NOT replace with assess_fluid_balance unless I/O totals/restrictions are stated.
- assess_fluid_balance: only if explicit I/O balance, urine output amounts/targets, strict fluid balance, daily weights, or fluid restriction is stated. Mentioning IV fluids alone is NOT fluid balance.
- assess_medications: only when specific meds/therapies are named or clearly identified (e.g., ondansetron, frusemide, dexamethasone, paracetamol, electrolyte replacement, “usual meds include…”). Vague “med review” without meds named => no label.
- assess_pathology: explicit lab/imaging/culture results OR explicitly pending/sent tests (e.g., “U&Es show hypokalaemia”, “stool sample sent”, “echo shows large effusion”, ECG findings).
- assess_nutrition: explicit diet/intake status (NBM, “tolerating sips”, general diet, restrictions).
- assess_pain: explicit pain presence/absence, pain score, discomfort, analgesia for pain, “pain controlled”.
- assess_mobility, assess_skin_integrity: only if explicitly discussed.

D) Recommendations / Plan (REC) — avoid over-labeling
- rec_plan: routine ongoing plan for shift/day (continue fluids, follow up results, prepare for procedure, continue diuresis/oxygen, monitor X routinely).
- rec_actions: ONLY if explicitly urgent/time-critical escalation or “must do now/STAT/call immediately if…” framing is present. If it’s routine “let me know if worsens” without urgency language, usually keep as rec_plan unless clearly time-critical.
- rec_discharge_plan: only if explicit discharge/transfer/placement planning is discussed.
- rec_patient_goals: only if explicitly asks for patient preferences/needs/goals (e.g., “anything you need right now?”, “what are your goals?”, explicit preference elicitation).

E) Introductions / Invitation / ID check (be very strict)
- introduction_patients: clinician introduces self to patient OR introduces patient at bedside (“Good morning Mr X, I’m Y and I’ll be your nurse”).
  - NOTE: “I’m handing over bed 4…” between clinicians is NOT introduction_patients.
- introduction_clinicians: clinicians explicitly introduce/identify each other as part of handover (“This is Evie taking over from me”).
- invitation: explicit permission/invitation for bedside handover or patient participation (“Is it okay if we do bedside handover?”, “jump in anytime”).
- id_check: ONLY if ALL THREE are explicitly checked: patient name + date of birth + an ID number/URN/MRN. Anything less => do not label.

COMMON PITFALL GUARDRAILS (based on prior errors)
- Do NOT label assess_fluid_balance when only IV fluids are mentioned; label assess_infusions instead.
- Do label assess_pathology when tests are sent/pending OR results are stated (stool sample sent, U&Es result, echo/ECG findings).
- Do label assess_nutrition when “tolerating sips” or any diet status is explicitly stated.
- Do label bg_history even when it is “no known medical history”.
- Do NOT label rec_plan just because someone says “documentation up to date”; only label rec_plan when a plan/continuation is explicitly stated.
- Do NOT label invitation/introduction unless the transcript explicitly contains those conversational elements.

FINAL STEP
Return ONLY: {"labels":[...]} with the applicable category keys.
