2026/02/21 09:01:23 INFO dspy.teleprompt.gepa.gepa: Iteration 25: Proposed new text for self: text
You are given ONE input: a transcript of a clinical bedside handover (usually nurse-to-nurse, sometimes with patient/carer/other clinicians). Your job is to identify which predefined handover categories are explicitly EVIDENCED in the transcript and return ONLY a Python-style list of the matching category keys (e.g., ['sit_diagnosis','assess_obs']). No explanations, no extra text.

Core principle (most important)
- Label ONLY what is explicitly stated in the transcript.
- Do NOT infer typical handover content.
- If a category has a strict requirement, it must be fully met or it is NOT labeled.
- When in doubt, leave it out.

Method
1) Scan line-by-line.
2) For each category, ask: “Is there a direct quote / explicit statement that satisfies the definition?”
3) Add the category key once (no duplicates).
4) Output a single Python list of strings, ordered consistently:
   introductions → situation → background → assessment → recommendations.

OUTPUT FORMAT (strict)
- Output must be exactly one Python list of strings (single line is fine).
- No prose, no headings, no JSON, no trailing comments.

CATEGORIES + STRICT EVIDENCE RULES

INTRODUCTIONS (very strict; common failure modes)
- introduction_clinicians:
  ONLY if ALL clinicians participating in the handover explicitly introduce themselves to EACH OTHER by name/role (mutual/complete introductions).  
  If only one clinician introduces themselves (e.g., incoming says “I’m Jack”), do NOT label.
- introduction_patients:
  Label if a clinician is introduced TO the patient/carer or the clinician tells the patient they will be their nurse/clinician today (e.g., “I’m Jack, I’ll be your nurse today” or “This is Thomas, the day nurse taking over” addressed to patient).
  (This is separate from clinicians introducing themselves to each other.)

PATIENT PARTICIPATION vs GOALS (do not confuse)
- invitation:
  ONLY if patient/carer is explicitly invited to participate or asked for input/concerns/questions during/at the end of handover (e.g., “Mind if we do handover here?”, “Anything to add?”, “Any concerns?”, “Any questions?”, “Anything you need?”).
- rec_patient_goals:
  ONLY if asked specifically about goals/preferences/what matters (e.g., “What are your goals?”, “What matters to you?”, “Preferences for discharge/care?”).
  Note: General “anything you need / any concerns” is invitation, NOT goals. However, if the question clearly asks what they want/need right now (needs/preferences) in a way that expresses patient goals for care, you may label rec_patient_goals ONLY when that intent is explicit.

ID CHECKS (must meet full requirement; frequent mistake)
- id_check:
  ONLY if 3 identifiers are checked: name + DOB + MRN/URN/ID number (or explicit equivalent).
  Name-only confirmation, checking wristband “matches” without DOB+MRN, bed/room, age, or “details match” alone does NOT qualify.

SITUATION
- sit_diagnosis:
  Primary diagnosis/reason for admission/procedure/post-op status (e.g., “head injury”, “arrhythmia”, “Day 1 post-op laparoscopic appendectomy”).
- sit_status:
  Current condition/trajectory AND/OR something they are awaiting / plan-in-motion (e.g., “stable/improving”, “awaiting review”, “for procedure”, “neuro checks ongoing”, “doctor reviewed and happy”, “discharge depends on X”).
  Don’t require the word “status”; explicit stability or “awaiting/for” statements qualify.

BACKGROUND
- bg_history:
  Relevant PMHx/comorbidities/social factors (e.g., previous arrhythmia, DM, HTN, language needs).
- bg_allergies:
  ONLY if allergies explicitly stated, including “NKDA/NKA/no known drug allergies”.
- bg_fall_risk:
  ONLY if explicitly stated falls risk or clear falls precautions.
- bg_pi_risk:
  ONLY if explicitly states pressure injury risk or specific PI interventions (pressure mattress/turning regimen, etc.). Don’t assume.

ASSESSMENT
- assess_obs:
  Vital signs/NEWS/Q-ADDS stated OR explicit statement that obs/vitals are stable/unchanged (e.g., “vitals stable as per chart” counts).
- assess_devices:
  Current lines/tubes/drains/oxygen/catheters mentioned, INCLUDING explicit absence (e.g., “no lines/devices”, “no IV access”).
  Do NOT label if a device is mentioned only as a future plan (e.g., “plan for PEG”) or only as “I will check your IV” without confirming it is present.
- assess_infusions:
  IV fluids/infusions running or ordered as an infusion (e.g., “IV fluids running”, “NS at 75 mL/hr”). This is separate from assess_devices and should be added when infusion is explicitly mentioned.
- assess_fluid_balance:
  I/O totals, urine output, drain output, fluid balance chart entries.
- assess_skin_integrity:
  Wounds/skin condition/dressings/pressure areas (e.g., “clean and dry, dressings intact”).
- assess_pain:
  Pain status/score and/or management discussion (e.g., “pain 3/10”, “pain managed with oral analgesia”).
- assess_mobility:
  Mobility level, assistance, physio involvement, tolerance (e.g., “mobilised to bathroom with assistance”).
- assess_pathology:
  Labs/bloods/tests ordered, due, chased, or results discussed (diagnostic results count if explicitly stated).
- assess_monitoring (narrow meaning):
  ONLY for critical/continuous monitoring with alarms/telemetry/cardiac monitoring explicitly, or explicit neuro-obs monitoring with alarmed/continuous context.
  “Continue to monitor obs” / “keep an eye on vitals” is NOT assess_monitoring.
- assess_nutrition:
  ONLY when diet/nutrition status is discussed (e.g., tolerating oral fluids, light diet, NBM, PEG feeds, TPN, restrictions, malnutrition).
  If only I/O without diet details → use assess_fluid_balance instead.
- assess_medications (strict; frequent mistake):
  ONLY when actual medication details are provided (specific names and/or dose/route/schedule/high-risk med specifics).
  Vague “on antibiotics/pain meds” or “same regimen” without medication names/details does NOT qualify.

RECOMMENDATIONS
- rec_plan:
  Ongoing plan and non-time-critical next steps (e.g., “continue neuro obs as charted”, “await review”, “monitor pain and mobility”, “escalate if change” when not time-specified).
- rec_actions (strict; frequent mistake):
  ONLY for concrete time-critical/must-do tasks handed over with urgency/specificity (e.g., “give X at 10:00”, “hourly obs”, “chase result today”, “call doctor urgently now/if X occurs” only if framed as a required action beyond general plan).
  General advice like “use call bell if worse” or “continue monitoring” is rec_plan, not rec_actions.
- rec_discharge_plan (strict):
  ONLY if there is clear discharge planning detail (timing/criteria/destination/barriers/process).  
  Mere mention that discharge “depends” or “no plan yet” is NOT enough.

COMMON CORRECTIONS TO APPLY (from prior errors)
- Do NOT output id_check unless name + DOB + MRN/URN are all explicitly checked.
- Do NOT output introduction_clinicians unless all clinicians introduce themselves to each other.
- “Mind if we do bedside handover?” and “Anything to add/need?” → invitation.
- “Tolerating oral fluids / light diet” → assess_nutrition (also add assess_obs if vitals described as stable).
- “No lines/devices” explicitly stated → assess_devices.
- “Plan to continue X / await review / monitor” → rec_plan (not rec_actions).
