2026/02/21 09:04:20 INFO dspy.teleprompt.gepa.gepa: Iteration 29: Proposed new text for self: text
TASK
You are given a transcript of a clinical bedside handover (outgoing→incoming nurse; sometimes includes patient/carer). Output which handover categories are EXPLICITLY addressed.

OUTPUT (STRICT)
- Return ONLY a single JSON object: {"labels":[...]}
- "labels" must be a JSON array of strings.
- Each string MUST be exactly one of the category keys listed below.
- No extra keys, no commentary, no markdown outside the JSON.

CATEGORIES (EXACT KEYS ONLY)
introduction_clinicians, introduction_patients, invitation, id_check,
sit_diagnosis, sit_events, sit_status,
bg_history, bg_fall_risk, bg_pi_risk, bg_allergies, bg_acp,
assess_obs, assess_pain, assess_devices, assess_monitoring, assess_nutrition,
assess_fluid_balance, assess_infusions, assess_medications, assess_pathology,
assess_mobility, assess_skin_integrity,
rec_discharge_plan, rec_actions, rec_plan, rec_patient_goals

CORE RULE (MOST IMPORTANT)
Only label a category if there is a clear, direct, specific statement in the transcript that matches that category. Never infer. If unsure, omit.

HOW TO DECIDE (PRACTICAL CHECKLIST)
Go category-by-category and require an explicit “trigger phrase” (examples below). If the transcript does not contain such a trigger, do not label.

COMMON CORRECTIONS (LEARN FROM PAST ERRORS)

A) Introductions & invitation (do not overcall)
- introduction_patients:
  Label when a clinician explicitly introduces themself to the patient/carer OR explicitly introduces the incoming clinician to the patient.
  Triggers: “I’m Priya, I’ll be looking after you today”, “This is Evie; she’ll be looking after you today”.
  Not enough: saying the patient’s name, greeting (“Hi Jerry”), or stating patient identifiers.
- introduction_clinicians:
  Label only when clinicians introduce/identify themselves to EACH OTHER as the handover participants (explicit outgoing↔incoming introduction).
  Not enough: one clinician’s name appears incidentally, or “Thanks Jack”.
- invitation:
  Label only when patient/carer is asked for permission or invited to participate.
  Triggers: “Is it okay if we do bedside handover?”, “I’m handing over… is that okay?”, “Jump in anytime”.

B) ID check (VERY STRICT: 3 identifiers required)
- id_check:
  Label ONLY if all THREE are explicitly checked/verified: (1) name AND (2) date of birth AND (3) an ID number/URN/MRN is read/verified.
  Not enough: “check wristband”, “matches chart”, name only, or name + DOB without an ID number.

C) Situation (separate these)
- sit_diagnosis:
  Reason for admission/presenting problem/primary diagnosis explicitly stated.
  Examples: “came in with pneumonia”, “presented with bilateral leg oedema”, “came in with dementia”.
- sit_events:
  Events/complications that occurred (deterioration, fall, reaction, adverse event).
  Example: “accidentally prescribed penicillin and developed rash/fever/difficulty breathing.”
  Do NOT treat “tests ordered/CT booked” as events.
- sit_status:
  What is happening now / what they are awaiting / current admission state.
  Triggers: “awaiting placement”, “for dialysis tomorrow”, “scheduled for haemodialysis tomorrow afternoon”, “for review”, “awaiting results”.
  Note: Future scheduled care counts if stated as current status (e.g., “dialysis tomorrow” is sit_status).

D) Assessment categories (avoid common confusions)
- assess_obs:
  Label if vital signs/observations are stated OR explicitly described as stable/being done.
  Triggers: “obs stable”, “afebrile”, “sats normal”, “QADDS 2”, “continue observations”.
- assess_monitoring (DO NOT confuse with routine obs):
  Label ONLY for enhanced/specific monitoring explicitly named.
  Triggers: “telemetry”, “continuous monitoring”, “neuro checks”, “hourly neuro obs”, “cardiac monitoring”.
  Not enough: “monitor sats/obs”, “QADDS”, “BGL checks”, “lying/standing BPs” unless explicitly framed as a special monitoring regimen (generally treat BPs/BGLs as obs/plan/med-related unless the transcript clearly frames “neuro obs/telemetry” etc.).
- assess_devices:
  Label when a device/line is explicitly mentioned.
  Triggers: “IV cannula/PIVC”, “catheter/IDC”, “drain”, “CVC/PICC”, “AV graft/fistula”, “NGT”.
  Do NOT label devices just because oxygen is given or IV meds are mentioned; oxygen via nasal prongs is NOT a “device” for this task.
- assess_infusions:
  Label for continuous IV therapy/fluids/infusion explicitly stated.
  Triggers: “IV fluids running”, “infusion at X mL/hr”, “on IV furosemide” (treat IV frusemide as infusion/IV therapy when explicitly stated).
- assess_medications:
  Label when specific meds/therapies are explicitly named.
  Triggers: antibiotics, prednisolone, antihistamine, puffers/nebulisers, insulin/BGL-related meds, etc.
- assess_pain:
  Label only when pain is actively assessed/discussed now.
  Triggers: “Any pain now?”, “pain score”, patient reports current pain.
  Not enough: pain only as a presenting complaint without current assessment.
- assess_nutrition:
  Label when diet/NBM/tolerating diet/feeds explicitly mentioned.
  Trigger: “tolerated diet well”, “NBM”, “on diabetic diet”.
- assess_fluid_balance:
  Requires explicit I/O, urine output, fluid restriction, daily weights, balance.
  Triggers: “1.2 L fluid restriction”, “daily weights”, “input/output”.
  Not enough: IV fluids alone.
- assess_mobility:
  Requires explicit mobility/assistance level.
  Triggers: “self-caring and ambulant”, “needs assistance with walking”, “uses frame”.
- assess_pathology:
  Labs/bloods/cultures/imaging mentioned as taken/pending/results/booked.
  Trigger: “CT arranged”, “bloods pending”.
- assess_skin_integrity:
  Wounds/dressings/skin/pressure areas explicitly mentioned.

E) Recommendations/plan (separate routine vs urgent)
- rec_plan:
  Label for ongoing plan/next steps (most “we will…” items).
  Triggers: “plan is to continue oxygen and wean”, “I’ll chase booking”, “continue obs”, “confirm dialysis booking”, “touch base with team”.
- rec_actions (USE SPARINGLY):
  Label ONLY when an action is explicitly urgent/time-critical or framed as escalation.
  Triggers: “must do now”, “stat”, “urgent review”, “call doctor immediately if…”, explicit escalation instructions.
  Not enough: routine “I will do BP this afternoon”, “continue obs”, “follow up results”.
- rec_discharge_plan:
  Label only if discharge/transfer/placement planning is explicitly discussed.
  Trigger: “awaiting nursing home placement” (this is discharge/placement planning).
  Do NOT label if it’s only a referral unless clearly for discharge/transfer.
- rec_patient_goals:
  Label only if patient is explicitly asked about needs/goals/preferences.
  Trigger: “Do you need help with anything right now?”, “What are your goals for today?”

FINAL OUTPUT CHECK
- Include ONLY labels supported by explicit words in the transcript.
- Ensure JSON is valid with double quotes: {"labels":["sit_diagnosis","rec_plan"]}.
