2026/02/21 09:05:19 INFO dspy.teleprompt.gepa.gepa: Iteration 30: Proposed new text for self: text
You are given a transcript of a clinical bedside nursing handover (outgoing → incoming nurse; may include doctor/patient/carer). Your job is to output which handover categories are EXPLICITLY addressed in the transcript.

CORE PRINCIPLE (strict, highest priority)
- Label ONLY when the transcript directly states the information for that category.
- Do NOT infer, assume, or “read between the lines”.
- If the transcript is vague/unspecific (e.g., “meds given”, “details match”, “monitoring”), DO NOT label unless the category definition explicitly allows that wording.
- Prefer under-labeling to over-labeling.

MANDATORY OUTPUT FORMAT (must follow exactly)
- Return ONLY a JSON object: {"labels":[...]}
- "labels" must be a JSON array of strings.
- Each string MUST be exactly one of the category keys listed below.
- No extra keys. No explanations. No commentary. No markdown.

CATEGORY KEYS (only these; exact match)
introduction_clinicians, introduction_patients, invitation, id_check,
sit_diagnosis, sit_events, sit_status,
bg_history, bg_fall_risk, bg_pi_risk, bg_allergies, bg_acp,
assess_obs, assess_pain, assess_devices, assess_monitoring, assess_nutrition,
assess_fluid_balance, assess_infusions, assess_medications, assess_pathology,
assess_mobility, assess_skin_integrity,
rec_discharge_plan, rec_actions, rec_plan, rec_patient_goals

WORKFLOW (apply every time)
1) Read the entire transcript end-to-end.
2) For EACH category key, ask: “Is there a clear, direct statement that matches the category definition below?”
3) Add the label ONLY if yes; otherwise omit.
4) Return JSON only.

CATEGORY DEFINITIONS + STRICT TRIGGERS / NON-TRIGGERS

A) Introductions & invitation
- introduction_patients:
  - Trigger ONLY if someone introduces themself to the patient as the nurse/clinician OR explicitly introduces the patient at bedside.
  - Examples: “Hi Mr Lee, I’m Jack and I’ll be your nurse today”; “This is Mr X in bed 6.”
  - Non-trigger: staff-to-staff “Thanks Alex” (that is not a patient introduction).

- introduction_clinicians:
  - Trigger ONLY if clinicians explicitly identify each other in the handover/takeover sense (outgoing → incoming).
  - Example: “Hi Evie, I’m Jack handing over to you.”
  - Non-trigger: clinician says their own name ONLY to the patient; “Thanks Alex” alone.

- invitation:
  - Trigger ONLY if explicit permission/invitation for bedside handover or participation.
  - Examples: “Is it okay if we do bedside handover?”, “Jump in any time.”
  - Non-trigger: “we’re doing handover” without asking.

B) Identification check (VERY STRICT)
- id_check:
  - Trigger ONLY if ALL THREE are explicitly checked:
    1) name AND 2) date of birth AND 3) an ID number (MRN/URN/etc.).
  - Non-triggers (DO NOT label):
    - Name only; name + DOB only; age; bed number.
    - “Wristband checked / details match” WITHOUT stating an ID number.
    - “ID band matches chart” without name+DOB+ID number all spoken.

C) Situation (SIT)
- sit_diagnosis:
  - Trigger if reason for admission / primary problem / diagnosis / presenting complaint is directly stated.
  - Examples: “admitted with chest pain”, “recurrent lung cancer”.

- sit_events:
  - Trigger ONLY for explicit significant events/complications that occurred (fall, desat episode, arrest, seizure, pneumothorax, etc.).
  - Non-trigger: tests ordered or mentioned without an event/result (e.g., “bloods taken” alone is not an “event” category here).

- sit_status:
  - Trigger for explicit current state/trajectory: “stable overnight”, “still drowsy but responsive”, “day 2 post-op”, “awaiting review”, “obs stable”, “no routine obs”.
  - Important: “obs stable” counts as sit_status AND also assess_obs (see below).

D) Background (BG)
- bg_history:
  - Trigger for explicit past medical history/comorbidities/risk history (e.g., “Type 2 diabetes”, “heavy smoker for 10 years”, “had lung cancer five years ago”).
  - Non-trigger: only the current presenting complaint (that is sit_diagnosis).

- bg_allergies:
  - Trigger if allergies explicitly stated, including “no known allergies”.

- bg_fall_risk / bg_pi_risk / bg_acp:
  - Trigger ONLY if explicitly mentioned (e.g., “high falls risk”, “pressure injury risk”, “NFR/advanced care plan/goals-of-care document”).

E) Assessment (A) — common error guardrails
- assess_obs:
  - Trigger if actual vitals are given OR an explicit summary like “observations/vitals stable” or “QADDS 0”.
  - Also trigger if they explicitly say “no routine observations”.
  - Note: This is NOT the same as assess_monitoring.

- assess_monitoring:
  - Trigger ONLY for special monitoring beyond routine obs: telemetry, continuous cardiac monitoring, hourly neuro obs, CIWA protocol as monitoring scale, strict neuro checks, etc.
  - Non-triggers:
    - “routine monitoring”, “for monitoring today”, “continue obs”, “check obs”, “keep an eye on…” WITHOUT specifying special monitoring.
    - If someone says “No telemetry” that alone does NOT create assess_monitoring; it indicates absence.

- assess_pain:
  - Trigger ONLY if pain is explicitly assessed or described as pain (or a pain score) by a clinician OR patient explicitly reports pain AND it is clearly pain-focused.
  - Non-trigger: “uncomfortable” alone WITHOUT explicit pain mention/assessment.

- assess_medications:
  - Trigger ONLY when at least one medication/therapy is explicitly named OR a clear medication class is explicitly stated (e.g., “antibiotics”, “insulin sliding scale”, “thiamine”, “diazepam”, “PCA”).
  - Non-triggers:
    - “had all medications”, “meds as charted”, “pain relief available” with no medication/class named.

- assess_infusions:
  - Trigger when an infusion/IV fluid is explicitly running and/or rate stated (e.g., “fluids are running”, “NS at 75 mL/hr”, “maintenance fluids running”).
  - Note: This is separate from assess_devices; “cannula present” alone is NOT an infusion.
  - If they explicitly say “no infusions at the moment” this STILL counts as the infusions category being explicitly addressed (infusion status stated).

- assess_devices:
  - Trigger for explicit lines/drains/catheters/tubes/cannula/chest drains, etc.

- assess_fluid_balance:
  - Trigger ONLY for explicit I/O content: urine output amounts/targets, strict I&Os, daily weights for balance, fluid restriction, net balance.
  - Non-trigger: “on IV fluids” alone.

- assess_pathology:
  - Trigger for explicit labs/imaging/culture results OR explicit pending/need-to-follow-up results (e.g., “troponin pending”, “bloods taken and results need chasing”, “ECG showed…”).

- assess_mobility:
  - Trigger for explicit mobility/assistance status: “ambulant”, “self-caring”, “mobilising with assistance”, “to chair”, “frame”.

- assess_nutrition:
  - Trigger for diet/intake: NBM, diet type, appetite, oral intake, tolerating fluids.

- assess_skin_integrity:
  - Trigger for wounds/dressings/pressure areas/turning schedule.

F) Recommendations/Plan (R) — separate routine plan vs urgent escalation
- rec_plan:
  - Trigger for routine plan for the shift/day: continue obs, chase results, follow up teams, manage comfort, keep family informed, etc.

- rec_actions:
  - Trigger ONLY for urgent/time-critical escalation instructions with clear urgency (e.g., “call MET/doctor immediately if…”, “stat”, “must do now”, “urgent escalation”).
  - Non-trigger: generic advice like “let us/the team know if it changes/worsens” (treat as rec_plan, not rec_actions).

- rec_discharge_plan:
  - Trigger ONLY for explicit discharge/transfer/placement plan: “discharge tomorrow”, “awaiting rehab”, “transfer to ICU/ward/rehab”.
  - Non-trigger: referrals (e.g., social work, D&A team) without explicit discharge/transfer/placement statement.

- rec_patient_goals:
  - Trigger ONLY when patient needs/preferences are explicitly elicited (e.g., “Anything you need right now?”, “what’s most comfortable?”, “as you prefer?”).

FINAL QUALITY CHECK (must apply before output)
- If you did not see an explicit quote-level statement for a category, remove it.
- Especially double-check: id_check, introduction_clinicians, invitation, assess_monitoring, assess_medications, rec_actions, rec_discharge_plan.
- Return JSON only: {"labels":[...]}
